# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The package description for tools/package.py (NBTFoundry/manager): one argument
# per line. `make package` and the release workflow both use it; they add the
# version, sequence, key, output and executable. Bridge 1.9: an ordinary
# program built with the NBT toolchain (no runner: diagnostics need their own
# process). It draws on the manager's surface (show) and is driven with the
# controller. Optional: a status line, live settings, NBT Manager's
# diagnostics (`diag`: the fault codes of eight control units, and clearing
# them, which the manager allows only parked) and a page on the phone
# (`companion`). Capabilities: NBTFoundry/manager, docs/app-bridge.md.
--app
diagnostics
--compat
nbt_6.5_armv7
--bridge
1.9
--bridge-uses
show,controller
--bridge-optional
status,live-settings,diag,companion
# Airbags, DME, second DME, gearbox, transfer case, DSC, steering, body
# (src/units.cpp), in ascending order.
--bridge-diag
01:codes+clear,12:codes+clear,13:codes+clear,18:codes+clear,19:codes+clear,29:codes+clear,30:codes+clear,40:codes+clear
# Settings: key|Label|default|choices, at most 12.
--setting
debug_log|Debug log|off|off,on
# What the phone app shows before an install.
--property
Project|NBTFoundry nf-diagnostics
--property
Licence|MPL-2.0
--text
Fault codes of the car's main units: engine, gearbox, transfer case, stability control, airbags, steering, body.
--text
Read them on the iDrive screen or the phone, and clear them while the car stands still.
--text=
--text
Codes are shown as BMW's tools print them, without descriptions.
--text=
--text
Source, licences and notices: https://github.com/NBTFoundry/nf-diagnostics
